{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1509926-the-dragonweaver-chosen-of-ah-ting","id":1509926,"title":"The Dragonweaver, Chosen of Ah-Ting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-27T22:37:39-07:00","id":1509926,"title":"The Dragonweaver, Chosen of Ah-Ting","content":"I'm makin' a thing. Anyone has advice or critiques, I'd appreciate it.<br /> <br /> <i>Ah-Ting, Architect of Harmonious Convergence, Surveyor of Essential Flows, God of Dragonlines</i><br /> Ah-Ting was a minor but influential god within the Department of Abstract Matters, a respected and well-liked personage since the early days of the Solar Deliberative. A skilled mapper of geomantic power and renowned for his insights into what harmonies would produce the best results, he was frequently called upon when a Manse was being raised or a Demesne seeded. The Sword of Creation saw a great deal of input from his office, both in his own notes and from his supervisor-child Erected Majesty, God of Manse Construction.<br /> <br /> Ah-Ting survived the Usurpation and the Great Contagion, despite frequent forays into Creation to remap shifting geomantic matrices. Early into the rise of the Realm, however, the god abruptly catalyzed an Exigence that rendered him all but dead. In the few moments of lucidity he has had since, Ah-Ting has maintained that he did so in response to the Sword of Creation`s use against the Seven Tigers and the subsequent disruptions to Creation`s geomancy. Without the Solars to address the finer issues and no Shogunate infrastructure to enact satisfactory spot-fixes, a specialist was needed. Rumors persist that the Exigent spark he used was illicit, procured from the Wyld-claimed Sanctum of slain a God by a Sidereal friend of Ah-Ting.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for Ah-Ting, the Dragonweaver Exaltation has been plagued with horrendously bad luck. The first so chosen was slain by marauding Fair Folk, and three subsequent incarnations were the targets of Wyld Hunts while making critical repairs in Realm war-manses. It is not helped by the fact that Erected Majesty holds no love for Ah-Ting's chosen, and would gladly destroy the Exaltation if it would reinvigorate their father. Only the fact that a Sidereal holds the mechanism for appointing a new Dragonweaver has kept Erected Majesty from making such an attempt, contenting themself with tipping off the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> Ah-Ting appears as a constellation of constantly repositioning, fist-sized prisms, enveloped by a cloud of glimmering slivers. This nebula of refraction surrounds a glowing core, the hue and intensity of which shifts based on the illumination the prisms feed into it. He now sleeps within his child Erected Majesty, a shivering cloud of astral dust dwelling in the stone-and-steel figure's hollow torso.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>The Dragonweaver, Chosen of Ah-Ting</b></u></span><br /> <i>Themes</i><ul><li>Geomancy, Dragonlines and Demesne</li> <li>Harmony and alignment</li> <li>Raw power; destructive if used abruptly but delicate and versatile if given proper guidance and time to work</li> </ul><i>Celestial-tier</i><ul><li>Adamant-Circle Sorcerer</li> <li>Cannot initiate into Necromancy</li> <li>Does not benefit from the Mastery keyword or suffer from the Terrestrial keyword.</li> </ul><i>Reincarnating</i><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Tied to a glass scepter, currently held by a Sidereal. The spark returns to the scepter when the current Dragonweaver dies, visible as a nacre flame dancing in the multifaceted head. New inheritors are chosen by being tapped with the scepter's head where a Caste Mark would be - those who pass a difficulty 3 Stamina + (Resistance or Occult) roll survive having their Essence pathways restructured, and assume the mantle. Failure destroys the candidate in an eruption of randomly-aspected Essence. Most candidates have been chosen from the unExalted members of a Heaven's Dragons Gens serving the Sidereal, with rumor being that Star-Touched are given special preference.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Dragonblooded lifespan, unaging when within a Demesne</i><br /> <br /> <i>Attribute-based</i><ul><li>Intelligence</li> <li>Stamina</li> <li>Perception</li> <li>1 Favored</li> </ul><i>Neutral with all Magical Materials</i><br /> <br /> <i>Anima</i><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">A shifting rainbow of chaotic energy, whose dominant colors and tones reflect what dragonlines are strongest in the immediate area. The Iconic Amina might depict a multi-hued tangle of serpents, a massive prism refracting the world around it, or a blinding swirl of scintillating dustmotes.</div> <br /> <br /> <i>Anima Effects</i><ul><li><u>Pluck the Threads</u>: for 1 mote, the Dragonweaver sends a pulse along the local dragonlines. This gives him a rough mental map of the geomantic makeup out to a radius of (Essence) miles, as well as giving a precise sense of direction towards the nearest uncapped Demesne within that area, if any.</li> <li><u>Ride the Dragon</u>: For 10 motes, 1 Willpower, the Dragonweaver can transport themself from one Demesne to another. This movement takes one scene regardless of distance, but only travels to the next Demesne \u201cdownstream\u201d along the dragonlines. If the Demesne feeds into multiple dragonlines, the Dragonweaver can choose which to traverse or simply allow fate to choose one at random. Manses cannot be transported into or out of, but will not impede movement along the line</li> <li><u>Blend With The Flow</u>: For 5 motes, the Dragonweaver can attune themself to any Demesne or Manse he is standing in for the rest of the scene. This is not contested by any owners, who by default are not alerted to the trespass.</li> </ul><i>Great Curse</i><br /> No limit track. Influenced strongly by the compositon of dragonlines in the immediate area. On Creation proper this mostly manifests in behavior similar to the relevant Dragon-Blooded aspect, but can result in highly paradoxical urges in areas with multiple powerful flows. In Heaven, Hell, and The Underworld, this results in stranger impulses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Charms</b></span><br /> <br /> <i>Crafting</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Forge of Creation<br /> Cost: 6m; Mins: Intelligence 3, Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One task<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> Tapping into an outpouring of Creation's Essence, the Dragonweaver infuses and reshapes the raw materials of their project through sheer will. Reality seems to warp around the construction - vines constricting metal to shape it, waves of heat scorching away excess paper, flows of water rearing in defiance of gravity to wear stone smooth, sunlight bleaching colors of unsurpassed hue into raw silk.<br /> <br /> Functions as &quot;Craftsman Needs No Tools&quot;, but only functions in either an uncapped Demesne or the Hearthstone room of a Manse. A Manse's aspect must be ontologically related to the craft (earth or fire for blacksmithing, wood or water for cooking, etc), while a Demesne`s unrestrained majesty can support any craft.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>Self-Modification</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Cultivation Of The Self<br /> Cost: \u2014(2m or 4m); Mins: Intelligence 3, Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> Every entity in Creation is composed of patterns of Essence, delicate pathways reminiscent of the dragonlines crisscrossing the land. The Dragonweaver reweaves her own Essence flows, channeling them into crystallized expressions of power.<br /> <br /> Upon purchasing this Charm, the Exigent chooses (Intelligence) hearthstones (including Linked stones). She can reflexively manifest one of these hearthstones as a jewel upon her brow, committing two motes for a lesser hearthstone or four motes for a greater hearthstone.<br /> Hearthstones that enhance weapons benefit her unarmed attacks. She gains the increased mote recovery for being in an attuned greater demesne (Exalted, p. 160). The hearthstones are indestructible but don\u2019t survive the Exigent\u2019s death. The Storyteller should veto hearthstone choices that are overpowered if made permanent, like the Gem of Incomparable Wellness. Hearthstones that teach Evocations have their first Evocation unlocked for free - subsequent Evocations must be bought with XP.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Gem of Many Facets<br /> Cost: \u2014 ; Mins: Intelligence 4, Essence 4<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cultivation of the Self<br /> <br /> Dragonlines connect all that is; everything, everywhere, all at once. The Dragonweaver can emulate but the smallest fraction of this expansive state of being, focused into a single point.<br /> <br /> The Dragonweaver can simultaneously manifest the benefits of Hearthstones created by Cultivation of the Self, each one slightly changing the hue and shape of the stone on their brow. Each stone adds their normal cost to the mote commitment.<br /> <br /> A repurchase at Intelligence 5, Essence 5 instead changes the cost to a flat 10-mote commitment to manifest their full library.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Harmonic Realignment<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Intelligence 3, Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Cultivation Of The Self<br /> <br /> The Dragonweaver enters the heart of a place of power, harmonizing the resonance between their Anima and the wellspring.<br /> <br /> The Dragonweaver chooses an Exalt type she\u2019s familiar with and a Caste or Aspect, causing her anima banner to take on an appropriate appearance and mimicking effects like the anima flux of the Dragon-Blooded. If she uses native Charms with overtly supernatural effects, they change to resemble the mimicked Exalt type\u2019s magic. She adds (Anima) dice on rolls with chosen Caste or Aspect\u2019s Attributes or Abilities and adds (Anima/2, rounded up) to static values based on them. If the Dragonweaver uses this Charm to emulate a Dragon-Blood, she can enter Elemental Aura using the Immaculate Dragon styles\u2019 Charms, letting her access the Immaculate Charms\u2019 Aura benefits.<br /> <br /> This Charm must be activated in a Demesne or Manse whose aspect marches the intended Exaltation - a Wood Manse for a Wood Aspect or a Sidereal Demesne for a Harbinger, for example. It can only mimic Exalts tied to Creation - Exaltations tied to forces from beyond, such as Gentimians, Dreamsouled, Infernals, Abyssals, Alchemicals, and Liminials, are not valid targets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On The Use Of Tuning Forks<br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Intelligence 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Harmonic Realignment<br /> <br /> Artifacts are crystallized points of power in and of themselves, merely not as blatant as a Demesne's outpouring. The Dragonweaver can now simply touch an appropriately-aspected Hearthstone or an Artifact that is Resonant to a given Exalt type to achieve their mimicry, rather than a Manse or Demesne.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Cross-Disciplinary Applications<br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Intelligence 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Harmonic Realignment<br /> <br /> All Essence, no matter how alien, shares the same fundamental structure. The Dragonweaver has delved deeply enough to mimic any Exaltation, so long as they have an appropriate fount of power at hand to harmonize with.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Places of Power<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Fount of Life<br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Stamina 3, Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> The Dragonweaver needs no base fodder to sustain him, so long as Creation\u2019s lifeblood is near. While within the confines of a Demesne, he does not need to eat, drink, or breath.<br /> <br /> A repurchase at Stamina 5 Essence 3 allows the Dragonweaver to receive this benefit so long as he is attuned to a Demese. Pseudo-attunements, such as that provided by Cultivation of the Self, do not count for this purpose.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Blessing of Auspicious Alignment<br /> Cost: 1m ; Mins: Stamina 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Fount of Life<br /> <br /> Striking key pressure points on a target, the Dragonweaver loans them a scrap of transcendence. As long as the mote remains committed, the target is treated as if they had the Fount of Life charm. The Dragonweaver can support up to (Stamina) such individuals at once.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ties That Transcend Boundaries<br /> Cost: 5m ; Mins: Stamina 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Fount of Life<br /> <br /> The Dragonweaver is above the crude \u201cattunements\u201d that other Exalts practice. As long this charm\u2019s motes remain committed, the countdown to when his attunement to a Demesne will lapse is suspended.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 05-13-2023, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T01:21:24-07:00","id":1509932,"title":"","content":"To do list:<ul><li>Great Curse</li> <li>Decide whether to keep it Attribute-based or switch to Essence-based</li> <li>More Charms (obviously)<ul><li>Social Charms that inflame wild bursts of emotion - emotional flavor can be chosen by the Dragonweaver if they're in Demesne -or have a Hearthstone- of a symbolically appropriate Aspect</li> <li>Rasing The Puissant Sanctum's &quot;natural Manse&quot; mode. &quot;Natural Manses&quot; count as Demesne for Dragonweaver Charms</li> <li>Direct damage Charm that has random aspect, or a specified aspect with access to the appropriate Demesne or Hearthstone. Can be upgraded to a ranged version</li> <li>Send out an apocalyptic pulse of power from a Demesne, damaging or destroying Manses within (Essence) [pending radius] and completely re-wiring the local dragonlines</li> <li>Create a Demesne. Only lasts as long as motes remain committed, unless a Sorcerous Working or Geomancy Major Project is undertaken. Can be of any Aspect the Dragonweaver has encountered before.</li> <li>Utility-belt Charm that gives little bonuses like auto-identifying Aspect/Caste/etc if they've studied it before</li> <li>Craft Charms related to geomancy, like raising, repairing, or destroying Manses.</li> <li>Be able to throw their senses around dragonlines</li> <li>Turn into a Demesne? Merge with one?</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 04-28-2023, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:",